  {
    "name": "fresh_route_redirects_to_pdf",
    "why": "A route with no cache entry: fetch, render, store, 302 to the PDF.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "do": "get",
        "path": "/roboviva/routes/123",
        "method": "GET"
      }
    ],
    "script": [
      {
        "status": 200,
        "headers": {
          "ETag": "W/\"v1\""
        },
        "body": "{\"route\": {\"name\": \"Probe Route\", \"course_points\": [{\"t\": \"Right\", \"n\": \"Turn right onto Street 0\", \"d\": 400.0}], \"metrics\": {\"distance\": 1609.344, \"ele_gain\": 100.0}}}"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "regeneration_runs_pdflatex_twice",
    "why": "THE DOUBLE RENDER. views.py:87 computes pdf_data, then views.py:102 calls latex2pdf(latex) AGAIN inside the open() block and writes that second result -- the first is discarded. Every cache miss pays for two full pdflatex runs. Almost certainly a copy-paste slip; pinned so the rewrite drops it deliberately.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "do": "get",
        "path": "/roboviva/routes/123",
        "method": "GET"
      }
    ],
    "script": [
      {
        "status": 200,
        "headers": {
          "ETag": "W/\"v1\""
        },
        "body": "{\"route\": {\"name\": \"Probe Route\", \"course_points\": [{\"t\": \"Right\", \"n\": \"Turn right onto Street 0\", \"d\": 400.0}], \"metrics\": {\"distance\": 1609.344, \"ele_gain\": 100.0}}}"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "unchanged_etag_skips_rendering",
    "why": "Second request with the same ETag: RideWithGPS answers 304, so no LaTeX and no pdflatex. This is what the cache is for.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "do": "get",
        "path": "/roboviva/routes/123",
        "method": "GET"
      },
      {
        "do": "get",
        "path": "/roboviva/routes/123",
        "method": "GET"
      }
    ],
    "script": [
      {
        "status": 200,
